<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons for Fire Mage DPS Phase 3</h2>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-and-two-handed-weapons-for-fire-mage-dps-phase-3">Main-Hand and Two-Handed Weapons for Fire Mage DPS Phase 3</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47518/mortalis">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_137.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mortalis</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47422/barb-of-tarasque">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barb of Tarasque</span></a> perform equally depending on your hit situation, but the former is likely to be less contested since less classes can use swords when compared to daggers. Because of this I recommend aiming for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47518/mortalis">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_137.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mortalis</span></a> and working with hit on other slots.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45620/starshard-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starshard Edge</span></a>, which was phase 2 best in slot, is now approximately 150 dps behind the two new best weapons - assuming best case scenario using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47470/mystifying-charm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_stratholme_a_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mystifying Charm</span></a> to drop hit. Past that, there's <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48013/sunreaver-disciples-blade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sunreaver Disciple's Blade</span></a> which is a more direct stand-in until you get <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47518/mortalis">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_137.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mortalis</span></a> if you plan to go that route, this weapon is close behind <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45620/starshard-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_92.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Starshard Edge</span></a> by 40-50 dps. Right after you have the option of either <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48701/spellharvest">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_137.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spellharvest</span></a> or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45990/fusion-blade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_132.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion Blade</span></a> which instead, are temporary items until <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47422/barb-of-tarasque">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barb of Tarasque</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>In terms of two handed weapons, you now have access to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47525/sufferance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_102.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sufferance</span></a> which sadly isn't all that great, it's more similar to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48013/sunreaver-disciples-blade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_shortblade_93.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sunreaver Disciple's Blade</span></a> rather than either of the 258 ilvl one handed weapons. It's also somewhat awkward to use as a temporary item since it provides no hit at all, and some mix of hit one-handed or off-hand tends to perform best this phase, creating the chance you might have hit issues later on in your gearing. Similarly, there's the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48036/illumination">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_102.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Illumination</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48045/perdition">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_102.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Perdition</span></a> staves, which are even worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47525/sufferance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_102.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sufferance</span></a> by a margin of 50-100 dps.<br/>
<br/>The <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> two-handed weapons also lose some value in comparison to phase 2, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45457/staff-of-endless-winter">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_94.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Staff of Endless Winter</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45886/icecore-staff">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_94.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icecore Staff</span></a> being worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47525/sufferance">
